  "text": {
    "intro": "The Mudflat Regatta is rowed over a course that is only a course at high tide, which is where most of the trouble starts.\nFour crews are involved. Determine each crew's placing, stroke and boat.\n- **Crew**: the Customs crew, the Seminary crew, the Creamery crew and the Almshouse crew.\n- **Placing** (listed from better to worse): first, second, third and fourth.\n- **Stroke**: Bartholomew, Crispin, Thomasina and Yusuf.\n- **Boat**: the Peregrine, the Wet Hen, the Gilded Eel and the Obstinate.\nEvery crew has a different placing, stroke and boat, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The crew who rows the Wet Hen finishes second.",
      "The crew who is stroked by Thomasina is exactly one place better than fourth, with no placing in between.",
      "The crew who rows the Obstinate is not stroked by Yusuf. The Customs crew falls somewhere between the crew who rows the Obstinate and the crew who rows the Wet Hen in placing order.",
      "The crew who is stroked by Crispin is exactly one place better than the Almshouse crew, with no placing in between. The Creamery crew is not stroked by Crispin.",
      "The Seminary crew does not row the Gilded Eel."
